Z||000000||Richard Parnell||05-22-2000||02:28 PM||||Does anyone know where I can get the proper slave cylinder for my hydraulic clutch system.  I need the small diameter 13/16 tubular type.  All the masters' I've found are 13/16 but every slave I've gotten has been a different size-none in 13/16.||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||05-22-2000||02:43 PM||||Richard, after looking around at all of the after market crap, myself, I went with a new GM unit.  For the 6 cyl, 5 spds, list was around $150.  However my local Pontiac dealer let me have one for the wholesale price, $114.  Yes, this is more expensive than some of the aftermarket brands, but it is not a cast iron unit.<P>I would check with your local dealer, and there is also that dealer in Maryland (I think), that WT3 always talks about (if not him its someone on here).  I think they are called Criswell Chevrolet, or something like that.<P>Hope this helps!<P>hoop||||reg||1
